f_snaps":58,"epa_per_play":0.07335,"pass_rate":0.6207,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6667,"def_epa_per_play":0.08402},{"week":15,"opponent":"MIA","home":true,"pf":20.0,"pa":12.0,"off_snaps":47,"epa_per_play":-0.1956,"pass_rate":0.6383,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6875,"def_epa_per_play":-0.2167},{"week":16,"opponent":"KC","home":false,"pf":19.0,"pa":27.0,"off_snaps":58,"epa_per_play":0.09239,"pass_rate":0.7069,"pass_rate_neutral":0.7143,"def_epa_per_play":0.1493},{"week":17,"opponent":"BAL","home":true,"pf":2.0,"pa":31.0,"off_snaps":54,"epa_per_play":-0.4148,"pass_rate":0.6852,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5,"def_epa_per_play":0.3111},{"week":18,"opponent":"TEN","home":false,"pf":23.0,"pa":14.0,"off_snaps":57,"epa_per_play":0.06263,"pass_rate":0.5088,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6111,"def_epa_per_play":-0.1846}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"DET","distance":0.5124,"shared":22,"play_caller":"John Morton"},{"season":2025,"team":"JAX","distance":0.5734,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Liam Coen"},{"season":2025,"team":"MIN","distance":0.5777,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Kevin O'Connell"},{"season":2023,"team":"DET","distance":0.5781,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2024,"team":"MIN","distance":0.6026,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Kevin O'Connell"}],"defense":[{"season":2021,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.5247,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Jeff Ulbrich"},{"season":2022,"team":"WAS","distance":0.744,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"PHI","distance":0.7986,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Jonathan Gannon"},{"season":2019,"team":"CLE","distance":0.7992,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"SF","distance":0.8423,"shared":22,"play_caller":"DeMeco Ryans"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Texans went 10-7 in 2024 and outscored opponents 372 to 372. The defense did most of the work, finishing 5th in EPA allowed while the offense ranked 22nd in EPA per play. Their most distinctive trait was the highest Cover 4 rate in the league.","offense":"The Texans offense was a little below average by EPA per play. They threw more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score did not call for it. C.J. Stroud ran the passing game, with Nico Collins leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Texans had one of the best defenses in the league, ranking 7th or better in four of the five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area was EPA allowed per rush, where it ranked 4th, and its weakest was explosive play rate allowed, where it ranked 19th. Will Anderson was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Danielle Hunter, who had 12 sacks, after not being a regular on this defense last season. In terms of scheme, they had the highest Cover 4 rate in the league.","special":"The Texans were one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 26% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers made 86% of field goals, which was a little above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the offensive line, about 24% of the money on the books. Their running backs were among the oldest in the league.","players":"C.J. Stroud played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 3,727 yards. Targets were spread around, with Nico Collins and Dalton Schultz leading a group where nobody took more than a fifth of the looks. Joe Mixon handled most of the work in the backfield with 65% of the carries. On defense, Danielle Hunter led the team with 12 sacks and Derek Stingley Jr. picked off 5 passes.","coaching":"Bobby Slowik called the offense and DeMeco Ryans called the defense. Their offense looked most like the 2025 Lions under John Morton and the 2025 Jaguars under Liam Coen. Their defense looked most like the 2021 Jets under Jeff Ulbrich and the 2022 Commanders.","trends":"The offense went from 15th in EPA per play in 2023 to 22nd in 2024, a modest decline. The defense moved from 13th in EPA allowed per play in 2023 to 5th in 2024, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was 22 personnel usage, which went from 4% to 0%.","notes":"Every data source is available for 2024. This season uses the newer formation labels, which group singleback, I formation and empty sets together as under center, so those older formation rates are not shown."}}